  "comment": "prism-qa bench projects (src/tools/qa/bench.cpp, docs/EVALUATION.md). Each project is fetched with git at `commit` (the pin; `tag` only names it). The `files` globs (`*` matches within one directory level) are copied into a scan tree, minus `exclude`; `generate` files are written there; and a compile_commands.json is written for the translation units (`*.c`, `*.cc`, `*.cpp` of the scan tree) with `std` (C) or `cxxstd` (C++), `include` and `define`. PRISM, cppcheck and clang-tidy all read that compile_commands.json.",
